        "model": "ChatGPT"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, head to Talampaya National Park in La Rioja Province.\n\nLike Ischigualasto, Talampaya is a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Fossils of dinosaurs, plants and early relatives of mammals have been found here. Ancient wetlands and lakes preserved traces of plant life.\n\nTalampaya Canyon is the park’s main natural attraction. Its cliffs rise about 150 m, and the canyon is around 80 m wide.\n\nVegetation is sparse, though there is a botanical garden within the canyon. Guanacos, red foxes, pumas and Patagonian hares are found around the streams and small rivers.\n\nAfter the tour, return to San Juan and transfer to your hotel.\n\n**Meals:** breakfast."
    },
    {
